# Content blocks

A content block is text used in more than one place, such as a notification template or a repeated hint. Write it once. Check it fits every place it appears.

<h2 id="wg-045">Keep notifications true and private</h2>

A notification must say what was observed, when, and nothing a stranger reading a lock screen should not see.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Nain is home alone and the back door is unlocked. | Back door reports Unlocked at 21:14. |
| Alarm triggered by Sam’s bedroom motion at 02:10. | Alarm triggered at 02:10. Open Home Assistant for details. |
| Door opened | Front door opened at 22:15. |

Put the time and the device in the first line. Keep personal detail out of the preview. Do not put passwords, tokens or exact addresses in a notification.

## Placeholders

When a block contains a value filled in later, name the value in capitals inside curly brackets. Check the sentence still reads well with a missing value.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| {{ states('x') }} opened | {DEVICE_NAME} opened at {TIME}. |
| (If DEVICE_NAME is empty) opened at 22:15. | Use a fallback: “A door opened at 22:15.” |
